ican, though Decision Desk HQ moved it to Toss-up in late September.\n\nPublic polling is sparse and largely hypothetical, but available averages put Donalds ahead by roughly four to six points, with one aggregator closer to one point. Prediction markets give Jolly about a one-in-four chance. The race has tightened enough to draw attention, but money, the state's partisan lean, and the ratings consensus still favor Donalds heading into the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1709, "margin": -5.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2654, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2923, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2636, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -4.5}]}